<Base
  title="Safety and compliance"
  description="How DBA equipment using R290 refrigerant is installed in Singapore, and which standards and guidance apply to flammable refrigerant equipment."
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Safety & compliance', href: '/safety-compliance/' }]}
>
  <header class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>Safety and compliance</h1>
    <p class="lede">Some of our newer models use R290, a natural refrigerant. This page explains what that means for installation in Singapore.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap prose body">
    <h2>About R290</h2>
    <p>R290 is propane used as a refrigerant. It has a very low global warming potential compared with the HFC refrigerants it replaces, which is why manufacturers are moving to it. It is also flammable, so equipment using it is designed, labelled and installed with that in mind.</p>

    <h2>Standards and guidance</h2>
    <p><strong>IEC 60335-2-40</strong> is the international safety standard for electrical heat pumps, air-conditioners and dehumidifiers, and includes requirements for appliances that use flammable refrigerants, such as limits on refrigerant charge relative to room size.</p>
    <p><strong>SCDF</strong> (Singapore Civil Defence Force) publishes fire safety requirements and guidance that apply to buildings in Singapore, including for equipment containing flammable refrigerants.</p>
    <p>Installation of our R290 models follows the applicable Singapore requirements and the installation instructions in each model's manual. Projects should check the current requirements with their qualified person or M&E consultant.</p>

    <h2>Installation</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>R290 units are installed by technicians trained to handle flammable refrigerants.</li>
      <li>The installer checks that the room and ceiling space meet the minimum size stated for the model.</li>
      <li>Servicing that involves the refrigerant circuit is done by trained technicians only.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Certifications</h2>
    <p>Certifications and energy labels are listed on each product page once they have been issued. If a certification isn't shown, please don't assume the model has it, and ask us for the current status.</p>

    <div class="note"><p>This page is general information, not legal or engineering advice. For project-specific requirements, consult the relevant authority or a qualified professional.</p></div>
  </div>
</Base>
